  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        email: "support@thespacedevs.com"
      }
      description: "The Launch Library 2 API provides access to a comprehensive database of rocket launches, space events, and astronauts. It serves both orbital and suborbital launches, offering data on launch service providers, events, agencies, and more, all accessible for free within certain request limits. Free tier allows up to 15 requests per hour."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Launch Library 2 API Server"
          url: "https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.2.0"
        }
      ]
      termsOfService: "https://thespacedevs.com/privacy"
      title: "Launch Library 2"
      version: "2.0.0"
      tagline: "Browse rocket launches, space events, astronauts, spacecraft and stations from TheSpaceDevs"
      homepage: "https://thespacedevs.com/llapi"
      docs_url: "https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.2.0/swagger"
      license_short: "Free tier capped at 15 requests/hour; higher rates via Patreon"
      license_md: `- Operated by TheSpaceDevs, a community project covering the space industry
- Free tier is rate-limited to 15 requests per hour
- Higher quotas are available to Patreon supporters
- Consult TheSpaceDevs site for current terms of use and attribution expectations`
      about_md: `Launch Library 2 is a REST API published by [TheSpaceDevs](https://thespacedevs.com/), a community project that catalogues the global space industry. The dataset powers a number of third-party launch trackers and dashboards.

What you get from the API:
- Upcoming and previous rocket **launches** with vehicles, pads, mission details and status
- **Agencies** (national space agencies and commercial operators)
- **Astronauts**, **expeditions**, **space stations** and **dockings**
- **Spacecraft** and **launchers**, including reusable first stages
- Space-related **events**, **locations** and launch **pads**

The server is \`https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.2.0\` and responses are JSON. The free tier is limited to roughly 15 requests per hour; sustained or higher-throughput use is intended for Patreon supporters.`
      entity_desc: {
        agency: "Space agencies and commercial operators that fund, build or operate missions."
        astronaut: "Human spaceflight participants with biographical details and mission history."
        docking: "Docking ports or interfaces between spacecraft and stations."
        docking_event: "Records of a spacecraft docking with or undocking from a space station."
        event: "Space-related events such as launches, landings, EVAs and mission milestones."
        expedition: "Long-duration crewed expeditions to space stations."
        first_stage: "Individual first-stage boosters used in launches."
        launch: "Upcoming and previous rocket launches with vehicle, pad and status."
        launch_vehicle: "Specific launch vehicle instances used for a flight."
        launcher: "Launcher (rocket) families and their configurations."
        location: "Geographic locations that contain launch pads."
        pad: "Individual launch pads at a location."
        reusable_first_stage: "Reusable booster cores tracked across multiple flights."
        space_station: "Crewed orbital stations and their operating status."
        spacecraft: "Crew- or cargo-carrying spacecraft and their flight history."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
